{"id": "11c1754c-9aed-467a-b4fe-28a5af23074a", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit the `nebula-demo-` roles against your live IAM quota values, checking attached managed policies, inline policy size, trust policy size, tags and role count. Then I'll build the remediation plan.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_GA2iyAOVGkc16mLOi6axMq", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "nebula-demo-iam-limits-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Audit all IAM roles whose RoleName starts with 'nebula-demo-' for objects approaching IAM limits, and return a data-backed list so a prioritized remediation plan can be built.",
  "context": "User wants a prioritized remediation plan using LIVE quota values (not documented defaults). Account: 012345678901_1 (agent space account; IAM is global, use region us-east-1 for Service Quotas / IAM calls). Read-only operations only - do NOT make any mutating calls. If other associated AWS accounts hold nebula-demo- roles, mention it but focus on the account above first (check list_associations if useful).",
  "resources": ["IAM roles with prefix nebula-demo-", "Service Quotas service code 'iam'", "iam get_account_summary"],
  "criteria": "1) Get live quota values: use service-quotas list_service_quotas (ServiceCode='iam') and/or get_service_quota to read applied values for: 'Managed policies per role', 'Role trust policy length', 'Role policy size' (inline aggregate size, if listed), 'Roles per account', 'Instance profiles per account', 'Customer managed policies per account', 'Policy versions in version control', 'Role session duration' and any other relevant IAM quotas. Also call iam get_account_summary (Roles/RolesQuota, Policies/PoliciesQuota, InstanceProfiles/Quota, AttachedPoliciesPerRoleQuota, PolicySizeQuota, PolicyVersionsInUseQuota etc.) and cross-check against Service Quotas; where they disagree, report both and state which is the live applied value. If a value cannot be fetched live, say explicitly that it's a documented default fallback. 2) Enumerate roles with prefix nebula-demo- (list_roles paginated, filter client-side by RoleName). For EACH role collect: count of attached managed policies (list_attached_role_policies), count and total character size of inline policies (list_role_policies + get_role_policy; compute size of the policy document JSON with whitespace removed as IAM does, note the aggregate-size method), trust policy (AssumeRolePolicyDocument) character length (whitespace stripped), number of tags (list_role_tags), and whether role is in an instance profile (list_instance_profiles_for_role). Also, for customer-managed policies attached to these roles, note policy document size vs PolicySizeQuota and the number of policy versions (list_policy_versions) vs the versions quota (typically 5). Also report the total count of nebula-demo- roles vs account Roles quota and overall account utilization. 3) Compute utilization % = used / live limit for every metric per role. Flag anything >=70% as 'approaching', >=90% as critical, 100% as at-limit. 4) Return a compact table of only flagged roles/objects (role name, metric, used, live limit, %), plus a short list of roles that are fine (just a count/names). Note any anomalies (e.g., trust policies with many principals/long lists, wildcard-heavy inline policies, unused roles via get_role RoleLastUsed that could be cleaned up). Keep the output concise; do not dump raw policy documents."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit nebula-demo- IAM roles against live IAM quotas"}], "created_at": null}

